flowchart TB
    accTitle: How get_connection reuses SQLite connections
    accDescr: A caller asks for a database path. If this thread already has a connection for that path it is returned. Otherwise the folder is created, a connection is opened with WAL, NORMAL sync, in-memory temp storage and a busy timeout, cached for this thread, and returned.
    A["get_connection(path)"] --> B{"This thread already<br>has one for path?"}
    B -- yes --> R["return cached connection"]
    B -- no --> C["create parent folder"]
    C --> D["sqlite3.connect<br>autocommit, Row rows"]
    D --> E["PRAGMA journal_mode=WAL<br>synchronous=NORMAL<br>temp_store=MEMORY<br>busy_timeout"]
    E --> F["cache for this thread"]
    F --> R
